WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.151
Two weeks later, the twins were sitting in the tree house.

2
00:00:06.152 --> 00:00:10.407
"How many eyes does a bee have?" asked Katie.

3
00:00:10.408 --> 00:00:13.131
Katie was reading a book about bees.

4
00:00:13.132 --> 00:00:15.971
Joy was brushing Jellybean.

5
00:00:15.972 --> 00:00:19.005
"Two," replied Joy.

6
00:00:19.006 --> 00:00:22.488
"Five," said Katie.

7
00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:26.504
She turned the page. "Okay," she said.

8
00:00:26.505 --> 00:00:30.702
"How many times does a bee flap its wings in a minute?"

9
00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:33.997
"A thousand?" guessed Joy.

10
00:00:33.998 --> 00:00:38.251
"Twelve thousand," Katie told her.

11
00:00:38.252 --> 00:00:41.645
Katie lay down and thought about bees.

12
00:00:41.646 --> 00:00:44.119
She imagined that she was a bee.

13
00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:48.160
"I'm a sleepy bee," she thought.

14
00:00:48.161 --> 00:00:50.287
Soon she was dreaming.

15
00:00:50.288 --> 00:00:54.446
She was Katie the Bee, flapping her wings.

16
00:00:54.447 --> 00:00:59.194
Other bees flew beside her, and she could hear their wings.

17
00:00:59.195 --> 00:01:02.434
"Katie!" cried Joy.

18
00:01:02.435 --> 00:01:04.475
Katie's eyes flew open.

19
00:01:04.476 --> 00:01:08.010
The pages of her book were flapping in the wind.

20
00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:10.101
Joy stood by the window.

21
00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:12.611
Jellybean was gone.

22
00:01:12.612 --> 00:01:16.777
"The sky is turning green ," Joy

23
00:01:16.778 --> 00:01:19.802
said. Dark clouds hung in the

24
00:01:19.803 --> 00:01:22.446
sky. Katie got up and looked at the wind

25
00:01:22.447 --> 00:01:26.295
sock. It was flying straight out in the

26
00:01:26.296 --> 00:01:29.352
wind. "A storm is coming," she

27
00:01:29.353 --> 00:01:33.352
said. She heard a rumble. "Thunder! Let's

28
00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:36.299
go." The girls hurried down the

29
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.479
steps. "Look!" shouted

30
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.151
Joy. "Grandpa is trying to get the chickens in their

31
00:01:42.152 --> 00:01:43.979
coop." The girls ran to

32
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.387
help. They chased the squawking

33
00:01:47.388 --> 00:01:52.682
birds. "Shoo!" they cried. Dust spun through the

34
00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:58.557
air. "Shoo!" One by one the chickens ducked through the coop

35
00:01:58.558 --> 00:02:01.403
door. "Run to the house," called

36
00:02:01.404 --> 00:02:04.234
Grandpa. "I'll be right behind

37
00:02:04.235 --> 00:02:07.452
you!" Mom was waiting on the back

38
00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:11.838
porch. "The weather service put out a tornado watch," she

39
00:02:11.839 --> 00:02:16.006
said. She held the door open and the girls rushed

40
00:02:16.007 --> 00:02:19.915
inside. The radio in the kitchen played soft

41
00:02:19.916 --> 00:02:22.991
music. "A tornado watch!" Katie

42
00:02:22.992 --> 00:02:25.724
cried. "We have to be on the

43
00:02:25.725 --> 00:02:31.067
lookout!" She grabbed her captain cap from a hook by the door and put it

44
00:02:31.068 --> 00:02:36.307
on. "This family is ready!" she declared as she went to the closet.

45
00:02:36.308 --> 00:02:41.177
She took a box from a shelf and carried it to the kitchen table.

46
00:02:41.178 --> 00:02:45.769
"Flashlight. First aid kit. Water. Snacks.

47
00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:49.523
Mom, are the pillows and blankets ready?"

48
00:02:49.524 --> 00:02:54.836
"Right here," said Mom, pointing to a basket under the table.

49
00:02:54.837 --> 00:02:59.220
"I wish Dad would come home," Joy said worriedly.

50
00:02:59.221 --> 00:03:04.881
Just as Grandpa opened the screen door, the music on the radio stopped.

51
00:03:04.882 --> 00:03:07.605
An announcer came on.

52
00:03:07.606 --> 00:03:12.656
"The National Weather Service has put out a tornado warning for Boone County.

53
00:03:12.657 --> 00:03:16.621
Current severe thunderstorms could produce a tornado.

54
00:03:16.622 --> 00:03:20.170
Towns in the warning include Willow Creek . . ."

55
00:03:20.171 --> 00:03:27.025
"A tornado warning!" shouted Katie. "That means TAKE COVER!"

56
00:03:27.026 --> 00:03:30.704
"I'll open the storm cellar," Grandpa said.

57
00:03:30.705 --> 00:03:35.631
Mom picked up her basket, and Katie picked up her box.

58
00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:39.047
"I've got the radio," said Joy.

59
00:03:39.048 --> 00:03:43.761
Outside a blast of rain and cool air hit them in the face.

60
00:03:43.762 --> 00:03:47.482
"It's so dark!" Katie said.

61
00:03:47.483 --> 00:03:53.033
"Dad!" shouted Joy as Dad's truck sped up the driveway.

62
00:03:53.034 --> 00:03:56.465
Grandpa held open the door to the storm cellar.

63
00:03:56.466 --> 00:03:59.259
"Hurry!" he called.

64
00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.159
"Magoo!" yelled Katie. "Come on, boy!"

65
00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.138
She and the dog dashed down the cellar steps.

66
00:04:07.139 --> 00:04:10.971
"Where's Jellybean?" cried Joy.

67
00:04:10.972 --> 00:04:14.670
Mom put an arm around Joy's shoulder.

68
00:04:14.671 --> 00:04:20.427
"Sorry, sweetie. There's no time to look for the cat right now," she said.

69
00:04:20.428 --> 00:04:23.820
"Oh, Jellybean . . . ," Joy whispered.

70
00:04:23.821 --> 00:04:27.924
Then she and Mom followed Katie down the steps.

71
00:04:27.925 --> 00:04:30.055
Grandpa was right behind them.

72
00:04:30.056 --> 00:04:35.107
Dad pulled the cellar door shut and fastened it tight.

73
00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:38.272
Magoo shook water from his fur.

74
00:04:38.273 --> 00:04:41.625
Mom grabbed blankets and pillows from her basket.

75
00:04:41.626 --> 00:04:45.143
"Take these," she said to the twins.

76
00:04:45.144 --> 00:04:49.415
They could hear the rain pounding on the cellar door.

77
00:04:49.416 --> 00:04:51.546
Katie hugged Magoo tight.

78
00:04:51.547 --> 00:04:54.629
Joy put a pillow over her head.

79
00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:59.259
Thunder exploded, louder and louder.

80
00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:02.177
Above them, the light bulb flashed.

81
00:05:02.178 --> 00:05:03.971
Everyone looked up.

82
00:05:03.972 --> 00:05:07.328
Then it went out.

